  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>S</mi></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math> be a twice differentiable function such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be defined as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>&#39;&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mn>5</mn></mfenced><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>&#39;&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to :</p>"
  },
